0..75 Comment "// No cloning in the type system: a qubit carries no comonoid, so no binder"
76..101 Comment "// copies or discards it."
102..104 Comment "//"
105..176 Comment "// A quantum state has no copy and no discard. A program that copies or"
177..252 Comment "// discards a qubit has no physical meaning, so the checker must refuse it."
253..255 Comment "//"
256..334 Comment "// A gate is a linear function from `Qubit` to `Qubit`, and it takes its qubit"
335..409 Comment "// once. A body that copies the qubit and a body that discards it are each"
410..482 Comment "// refused by name. A binder that may use a qubit any number of times is"
483..559 Comment "// refused too, whether a function, a declaration or a data field writes it."
560..562 Comment "//"
563..613 Comment "// - see: `../../ledger/features/qubit-type.gandr`"
615..660 Comment "// The qubit type, which carries no comonoid."
